title FUSS-J14r2 — comlink device-guest prose relabeled, guard widened to 17 surfaces
prompt Continue the autonomous loop: climb FUSS-J14r2 (the comlink guest cluster), send as its own signed round.
think r1 proved the meaning-preserving relabel discipline on amphora. r2 takes the largest single cluster — the comlink device guests carrying a bare lap ordinal beside a structured code (OA-L3 lap 2, I2 snapshot lap 3, NS-L3 wire lap 2, Amphora lap 3), plus comlink/README.md's three bare-ordinal port-table labels.
think Scoped the worklist to exactly the sixteen guest_*.rye the VOLS ledger names as prose gaps — the ones where grep -cPi of the bare-ordinal pattern returns 1. The other ~44 comlink guests already use law-permitted structured codes (OA-L2, OA-L5, sub-lap, SLC-L2, MUR M2b, catch-up, two-way, Granary lap 4b, Tablecloth query) and are NOT in the 79.
think First attempt overreached — a comlink/guest_*.rye glob matched all ~60 guests and a newline-eating regex (s/\.\s*$/…/) merged line 2 into several headers. Caught it immediately in the dry-run output (files showing ·20260713.//! = eaten newline), reverted the whole comlink dir with git checkout, and redid on the explicit 16-file list with a newline-preserving regex (s/\.(\s*)$/ … .$1/) that captures and restores the trailing whitespace. Verified exactly 16 guests changed, each a single-line diff, wc -l unchanged.
think The relabel drops the bare " lap N" token (redundant beside the structured code) and appends · 20260713 (every guest's own git author date). The structured code (OA-L3/I2/NS-L3/Amphora) and the device role survive, so no capability loses its name. README rows named by device (Snapshot device · Amphora vessel fetch · Granary resin serve), port numbers untouched.
obs The guest binaries are byte-unchanged in behavior — a //! doc-comment header is never printed, so the qemu/virtio device-wire witnesses (which the sandbox cannot run anyway) are untouched; only prose moved. This is why comlink was safe to relabel even though its witnesses stay env-gated.
obs Added all 17 relabeled surfaces (16 guests + comlink/README.md) to labeling_module_scan.sh; CION guard GREEN over the widened set (verdict=ok on the swept set, verdict=drift on the negative fixture — the bite). guarded_sites climbs 3 → 20 of 79. width-check exit 0, tame_style_check GREEN.
file comlink/guest_open_asks_escrow_hold_rx.rye … (16 guests) header relabeled: bare lap ordinal dropped, structured code + device role + stamp 20260713 kept
file comlink/README.md three port-table labels named by device (Snapshot · Amphora vessel fetch · Granary resin serve), no bare ordinal
file tools/gen/season/cion_module_labeling_witness.rish grew the scan list by the 17 comlink surfaces; header comment + GREEN line record the sweep; guard GREEN
recommend keep-going FUSS-J14r3 — the voice and market modules (ember · lantern · lattice · mandi · greencandy · glow/nock READMEs and authored .rye prose): relabel each to semantic label + stamp, grow the guard, GREEN
